* BYEBYE - STOP THE LOCAL EMULATOR

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* BYEBYE - STOP THE LOCAL EMULATOR

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:BYEBYE

Halts cpmsim and returns to the host terminal. Use only after the caller
has logged off and guest writes have finished.

This is the local shutdown command. Public BYE logs off a caller instead.
After the halt message, the host updater can safely acquire the
installation lock.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
